247-Keep these maintenance control families direct in the runtime surface:
248-- runtime owner integrity
249-- chapter-family answerability
250-- document-benchmark to assembled-replay escalation
251-- route choice between staying document-grounded vs escalating to behavior proof
252-
253:Default route policy for this maintenance class:
254-- primary route: stay at document-level benchmark while the live question is doc/runtime parity, chapter-family answerability, or benchmark coverage
255-- fallback route: escalate to assembled replay when ambiguity, conflict, or behavior-critical claims need stronger evidence than document-grounded review can provide
256-- final ownership reroutes to `eval-ops` once the decision depends on replay execution state, benchmark gating, or release-sensitive continuation rather than route comparison alone
257-
258-Direct family note:
259-- for `runtime owner integrity` and `benchmark-loop adequacy`, document-level benchmark is the primary sufficient surface when runtime-owned docs directly expose the owner boundary or benchmark loop
260-- replay escalation is not required for those families unless the claim extends from document/runtime parity into assembled behavior proof or runner execution state
261-
262-Escalate to stronger operational artifacts when:
263-- document parity is no longer the live question and assembled prompt behavior must be replayed
264-- scenario lineage, run linkage, or replay execution state must stay inspectable across reruns
265-- the verdict depends on whether a replay actually executed rather than whether a benchmark question set exists
266-
267-Preferred operational artifacts:
268-- `Benchmark cohort manifest` when scenario identity and expected replay contract must be fixed before execution
269-- `Replay runner verdict sheet` when runner state, partial completion, or replay-attempted vs replay-complete distinction is the live issue
270-- `Replay suite verdict memo` when a higher-level suite verdict must summarize multiple runner-linked replay outcomes without hiding partial coverage
